    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Probe a local audio, image, or video file and return stable technical metadata.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input audio, image, or video file path.\r\n          --field TEXT:{size_bytes,width,height,coded_width,coded_height,rotation_degrees,duration_us,fps,container_format,image_format,image_codec,video_codec,has_audio,audio_codec,sample_rate_hz,channels} \r\n                              Result field to return. Repeat once per field.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media probe --input /tmp/in.mp4\r\n  $ lyra-cli media probe --input /tmp/photo.jpg --field width --field height --field image_format\r\n  $ lyra-cli media probe --input /tmp/in.mp4 --field duration_us --field fps --field video_codec\r\nNOTES\r\n  Without --field, returns all stable fields available from the current platform backend.\r\n  Repeat --field for strict projection; unavailable requested fields fail instead of being omitted.\r\n  operator, input, and type are always returned.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Probe a local audio, image, or video file and return stable technical metadata.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input audio, image, or video file path.\r\n          --field TEXT:{size_bytes,width,height,coded_width,coded_height,rotation_degrees,duration_us,fps,container_format,image_format,image_codec,video_codec,has_audio,audio_codec,sample_rate_hz,channels} \r\n                              Result field to return. Repeat once per field.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media probe --input /tmp/in.mp4\r\n  $ lyra-cli media probe --input /tmp/photo.jpg --field width --field height --field image_format\r\n  $ lyra-cli media probe --input /tmp/in.mp4 --field duration_us --field fps --field video_codec\r\nNOTES\r\n  Without --field, returns all stable fields available from the current platform backend.\r\n  Repeat --field for strict projection; unavailable requested fields fail instead of being omitted.\r\n  operator, input, and type are always returned.\r\n",
